     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Washington Jones and Pham Clinic\nPatient: Lisa Whitehead DOB: 08/19/1946 Sex: F MRN: 586374\n\nEncounters:\n 2026-06-19 Vitamin D deficiency BP 141/79 Wt 159\n 2025-01-27 Insomnia only BP 150/86 Wt 160\n 2023-09-07 Medication refill BP 146/86 Wt 145\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • Insomnia only - Lisa has been managing her insomnia using zolpidem 5 mg and trazodone 50 mg. These medications have helped improve her sleep quality and duration, allowing her to feel refreshed and alert during the daytime.\n • Osteopenia - Lisa's osteopenia is under control with alendronate 70 mg. This medication helps maintain bone and reduce the risk of fractures. Regular monitoring and follow-up are scheduled to ensure the condition remains stable.\n • Vitamin D deficiency - Lisa's vitamin D deficiency is being managed with ergocalciferol 50000 IU. Her recent follow-up visit showed that her vitamin D levels are improving, and her bone health is stabilizing. We will continue to monitor her levels and adjust the dosage as needed.\n\nAdditional Notes:\n- Lisa has been compliant with her prescribed medications and has not reported any side effects.\n- Her blood pressure readings have been within the normal range during recent visits, with the latest reading being 141/79 mmHg on June 19, 2026.\n- Lisa's weight has remained relatively stable, with a recorded weight of 159 pounds on June 2026.\n- Lisa currently uses a vape product daily as part of her tobacco habit. She disclosed this use honestly during our last visit on June 19, 2026.\n\nExamination Findings:\n- Vital signs during recent visits have been within normal limits, with heart rates, respiratory rates, and temperatures all falling within expected ranges.\n- General physical exams, including head, eyes, ears, nose, throat, respiratory, abdominal, and neurological exams, have shown no significant abnormalities.\n- Musculoskeletal exams have confirmed no signs of fractures or significant joint pain, consistent with stable osteopenia.\n\nSocial History:\n- Lisa is currently using a vape product daily, which she disclosed during her last visit. She has been honest about her tobacco use and has not shown intention to quit at this time.\n\nOverall, Lisa is managing her chronic conditions effectively with her current medications. She is compliant with her treatment plan and has shown no signs of complications. Regular follow-up appointments will continue to ensure her conditions remain stable and well-managed.\n"
